  "notes": "LA's self-producing melodic-rap singer — the 2020s \"soul back to LA\" record, and the tightest tempo band in this batch (93–105, almost nothing above 115). Three researched parameters do the work. ⚠ **\"An effortless drum pocket\" is a timing instruction.** The research says the clap/snap sits \"slightly behind the grid\" with \"a soft and-of-3\" and \"16th hats low in the mix\" — so `snare.offGridMs` is 8 with a 4–9 ms clap layer behind it, the kick's `lockTo808` drops to 0.5, and `hihat.velocities.main` falls to 0.50–0.72, which is the quietest hat lane in this batch. The \"cricket-like chirps\" that replace the hat are the foley `percs` lanes. ⚠ **He produces his own records, and the research makes that a MIDI-facing parameter**: \"the chord bed and the vocal are written together, so the top-line sits *inside* the voicing rather than above it.\" So `melody.register` (55–79) deliberately overlaps `chords.voicing.register` (48–76) instead of sitting above it, and `chordToneBias` is 0.88 — the highest here. That overlap is the entry's signature and is not a mistake. ⚠ **The harmony has real motion**, which most of this lane does not: the research names `i–iv–VII–III` and `Imaj7–vi7–ii7–V` specifically, so both are authored as families and `extensions` runs 0.20 triad / 0.50 seventh / 0.30 ninth for the \"warm minor with major-7th colour\". The 808 is \"rounded ... never distorted, never the loudest element\": `distortion` none, `slideProb` 0.4 for the \"slow portamento following the piano's root motion\". Arrangement follows \"sung hook first, 12–16-bar sung-rapped verses, harmony-stack pre-hook, drumless piano tag\" and his stated principle that \"quality outlasts quantity\". ⚠ `confidence` is `high` on the research's \"high-medium\". **The inferred parameter is `percs.densityPerBar`** — \"small foley-percussion details\" is a description of texture, and how many per bar is a reading of it. Fill fingerprint band G. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.5 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.5 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
